WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
Look inside a charging cable:
copper wire in the middle,

2
00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.510
plastic all around it.

3
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.920
Put the same voltage across each.

4
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.800
The copper carries a current.

5
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:12.370
The plastic carries almost none.

6
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.020
On a resistivity scale, copper sits
at just 17 billionths of an ohm-metre.

7
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.840
Plastics sit far, far higher.

8
00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.850
Same voltage, utterly different results.

9
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:26.700
So what makes such an enormous difference?

10
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:30.340
In this mission, you'll look
inside a metal and a salt solution,

11
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.710
and ask what actually
moves when a current flows.

12
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.420
Then you'll compare conductors,
semiconductors and insulators on one scale of

13
00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:39.750
resistivity.

14
00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.750
Your mission: explain what makes copper
conduct so much better than plastic.
